    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Nj63G7ZhArAdRaWCoEmS1p)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Independent of the open PRs; touches only `sp-bibprocess` (docs in `sp-academic.org`, tangled `.el`, tests).\n- It does not change `sp-batch-report`, so it should not conflict with the batch-report rebuild; the report section is plain Org text added next to the existing ones.\n\n## What\n\n- Adds step 4 to `sp-bibtex-lint-fix-authors`, also `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-fix-merge` and \"merge author names\" in `sp-bibtex-lint-convert`.\n- Finds variants of one person in the `.bib` file: same surname (accents, case, braces, dots ignored) and given names that fit name by name (`Hegel, G. W. F.` / `Hegel, Georg Wilhelm Friedrich`, `Müller` / `Muller`), using the matching of the litnote autofill.\n- A name that fits two names that do not fit each other (`Hegel, G.` for Georg and Gottfried) is never merged, only listed.\n- Proposed name: an author-note name if a variant is one, else most spelled-out given names, then most used.\n- Dry run: `sp-bibtex-lint-dryrun` has a new section \"Variants of one author\" with the groups, counts and proposed name; nothing is written.\n- Fix: shows the groups, asks for each (RET proposed, edit, `-` skip, `C-g` stop), one yes-or-no question, backup, one write.\n- Only names are replaced in `author` and `editor`: order, `and` separators, quotes or braces and other names stay. Entries with a comment inside are left alone.\n- Author notes and litnotes are not touched (separate optional step).\n\n## Not done / notes\n\n- Spelling variants such as `Smyth` stay with the existing note-typo step.\n- The report section scans the file synchronously, so the dry run may pause on a very large `.bib`.\n- Branch is `claude/project-thread-ti8dcv`: the cloud proxy cannot rename a branch, so it needs the number prefix from Sia.\n- Tests: 78 pass in batch Emacs 29.3 (`tests/sp-bibprocess-lint-test.el`, 5 new). Not run on the real `.bib` files.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-dryrun` on a real `.bib`: section \"Variants of one author\" lists plausible groups, with the proposed name first\n- [ ] Check a group that should not merge (two people with the same surname and initial) is absent or listed as \"not merged\"\n- [ ] `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-fix-merge`: accept one group, edit the name of another, skip a third with `-`\n- [ ] After the write, `git diff` of the `.bib` shows only names replaced, same author order, same `and` separators, braces intact\n- [ ] Entries with a comment inside are unchanged\n- [ ] A backup copy exists in `sp-bibtex-lint-backup-directory`\n- [ ] `C-g` during the questions leaves the file unchanged\n- [ ] `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-fix-authors` runs the four earlier steps and then the merge step\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiD4sbuQPYY3vLSVmkK)_",
